CharacterizationRule.Notes:
To cover usage of the '<<' operator with stringstream objects such as:
               basic_stringstream<char> stringStream;

               stringStream << tainted;

CharacterizationRule.Definition:
foreach taintfrom {
    TaintTransfer(taintfrom, taintto)
}

CharacterizationRule.Notes:
Required for SCA to understand that in statements like:
                stringStream << "something" << tainted;

                The chained '<<' operators will all operate on the same underlying stream

CharacterizationRule.Definition:
{std,std::,std::__1} / "operator<<"(stream, input) {
    Returns(stream)
}

