In this case, an improperly constructed format string causes the program to access values outside the bounds of allocated memory.

<b>Example 1:</b> The following reads arbitrary values from the stack because the number of format specifiers does not align with the number of arguments passed to the function.
<pre>
void wrongNumberArgs(char *s, float f, int d) {
   char buf[1024];
   sprintf(buf, &quot;Wrong number of %.512s&quot;);
}
</pre>

